aragon-ai (1.5.25) stable; urgency=medium

  * Fixed web search (and news/images/videos/page-fetch) going down after a
    routine restart: the search bridge depended on a third-party package
    with no upper version limit, so picking up that package's latest
    release could silently break it. It's now pinned to a known-good range,
    and a separate port mix-up that could only surface once that crash was
    fixed is also corrected.

  * Fixed "how many nautical miles" style unit conversions being rejected
    ("nmi" was not recognized as a unit).

  * Hardened every other place in the installer that downloads a dependency
    without a fixed version — Home Assistant rules, the Spotify voice
    module, the search engine itself, the Sonos integration, and the core
    agent and voice-tool services. All of these now install the exact,
    tested version every time, including on a routine update to an
    already-running device, so a change on the internet can no longer
    silently break something that worked yesterday.

